From: Kervin Pursoty <kpursoty@proton.me>
Subject: net: econet: add EcoNet SoC Ethernet driver

Add the EcoNet Ethernet driver supporting EN751221, EN751627, and EN7528
SoCs. The driver supports 2 QDMA engines and 2 GDM ports with an
internal MT7530 GbE switch operating in dumb-switch mode.

EN751627 uses en751221_soc_data (big-endian, dscp_byte_swap=true) since
both SoCs share the same FE/QDMA architecture.

Driver originally by Caleb James DeLisle <cjd@cjdns.fr>.
EN751627 support added by Kervin Pursoty <kpursoty@proton.me>.

Signed-off-by: Kervin Pursoty <kpursoty@proton.me>
---

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/Kconfig
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here. The module
 	  will be called ec_bhf.

+source "drivers/net/ethernet/econet/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/net/ethernet/calxeda/Kconfig"

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/Makefile
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_NET_VENDOR_CIRRUS) += cirrus/
 obj-$(CONFIG_NET_VENDOR_CISCO) += cisco/
 obj-$(CONFIG_NET_VENDOR_CORTINA) += cortina/
 obj-$(CONFIG_CX_ECAT) += ec_bhf.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_NET_ECONET)		+= econet/
 obj-$(CONFIG_DM9000) += davicom/
 obj-$(CONFIG_DNET) += dnet.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_NET_VENDOR_DEC) += dec/
